  "example_content": [
    {
      "text": "Important legal context on the ICJ provisional measures: 'plausible' in ICJ procedure means the court found sufficient evidence that the rights claimed (protection from genocide under the Genocide Convention) are at least plausible. It's NOT a finding of genocide \u2014 that comes at the merits stage, which could take years. But it IS significant: the court doesn't issue provisional measures unless it believes there's a genuine risk the rights at stake could be irreparably harmed.",
